    <h2>Further reading — not the law</h2>
    <p>
      <a
        href="https://www.livinginandorra.com/residency_options.html"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Living in Andorra — residency options 2026</a
      >
      (Jane Whittaker, J W Serveis). Use it to see how an English-speaking
      practitioner groups files. Then return to the official links above.
    </p>

    <h2>Who can help</h2>
    <p>
      Most files are prepared with a local gestoria or law firm, a bank, and
      often an AGIA-registered estate agent for the housing certificate. We list
      only organisations with an official website.
    </p>
    <p>
      Start with
      <a href="/directory">the directory</a>
      —
      <a href="/directory/jane-whittaker">Jane Whittaker</a>,
      other residency and tax counsel, the three Andorran banking groups,
      clinics, and licensed agents. For housing itself, see
      <a href="/buying-property">buying as a non-resident</a>,
      <a href="/properties">properties</a>
      and the
      <a href="/parishes">seven parishes</a>.
      Country notes:
      <a href="/moving-to-andorra-from-the-uk">UK</a>,
      <a href="/moving-to-andorra-from-spain">Spain</a>,
      <a href="/moving-to-andorra-from-france">France</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you would like an introduction rather than a cold approach, register
